              "text": "4.25–26",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "feet",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": ": This reference to “feet” is thought by some to be a euphemism for the genitals.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " with it. Because of the rite of circumcision she said to Moses, “You are a husband of blood to me.” And so the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.4.25+EXO.4.26",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.4.25",
              "EXO.4.26"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " spared Moses' life.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.4.25+EXO.4.26",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.4.25",
              "EXO.4.26"
            ]
          }
        }
